learnings:
  - Team-led fixes catch related bugs the original report misses. Jinx's audit found aspect_drift had same bug; shared helper closed both in one PR. Solo-Claude likely would have shipped Option B for aspect_check only.
  - Shared resolver helpers are architectural insurance against writer/reader drift in MCP tool pairs. Without one, every tool implementing path resolution is a future drift opportunity.
  - The MISSING roundtrip integration test was the process gap that let this bug ship. Writer self-verification only checks YAML write, not reader resolvability. Roundtrip tests for every writer/reader MCP pair should be a category requirement going forward.
